                      %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
                               CENTERLINES.GAWK
                      ONE CENTER SCRIPT TO RULE THEM ALL
                      %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

Usage:  $ ./centerlines.gawk -v w=[0-9]+ <stdin
        w controls line character width (default: 79)

$ ./centerlines.gawk -v w=50 <<< "this line is now centered"

            this line is now centered

Can be easily integrated into nano or vim:
  # .nanorc
  unbind F4 main
  bind F4 "{execute}| centerlines.gawk -v w=79" main
